# UI craft — ProductName Spatial Instrument

When changing workspace or dock UI, read and obey:

1. [`docs/design/spatial-instrument-brief.md`](docs/design/spatial-instrument-brief.md) — numbers, anatomy, anti-examples
2. [`design-system/productname/MASTER.md`](design-system/productname/MASTER.md) — tokens in the running app
3. [`docs/design/ambient-dock-ui.md`](docs/design/ambient-dock-ui.md) — Peek geometry only

## Must

- Student-beta is a **real workspace window** (D-11). Peek is still not a dashboard.
- Glass on chrome (sidebar, sheets, palette, now-playing). Opaque `--surface-2` for study prose and lists.
- Tokens from brief §6: `--bg`, `--surface-0/1/2`, `--surface-grouped`, `--accent` cobalt, radii 20/24/16/12/pill.
- Dual density: tight lists vs 44px iOS controls vs 17px study reading. Do not average.
- Four themes: Paper Solare cream, Night `#1C1C1E`, Forest pine + cream (not mint), High contrast `#0E0E10` no blur.
- Source Serif 4 + IBM Plex Sans/Mono. Squircle mark; no “PN”.
- Hit 44×44. Focus `2px --ring` offset 2. No `outline: none` on controls.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` and `data-motion="reduced"`. Never `transition-all`.

## Must not

- 8px default control radius in the workspace; 13.5px root type; 168px bordered tab rail
- Forest mint `#7fd1a0`; Paper cool-white `#FAF8F3`; Night navy-black `rgb(12,16,24)`
- Purple/indigo/cyan glow; Inter/Geist/Roboto; emoji icons; 3-up feature cards
- Full Liquid Glass on paragraph text; Brik motion on tabs/settings/calendar
- Microphone / ASR; restyling Peek as visionOS panels unless tokens leaked
